 "profile_note": "Backend / data / AI-leaning software engineer and published researcher. Master's in CS (EPN, 2026). Industry: Thoughtworks (Java, C#, Node.js/NestJS, PostgreSQL, Neo4j, Redis, TDD, client-facing consulting; also evaluated AI-generated code for LLM training), Llacsaa junior developer. Research: ADA Lab research technician 2023-2025; 6 peer-reviewed publications (ORCID 0009-0002-5080-9126) on polyglot persistence and data pipelines: PolyFuseQL (federated queries over SQL/NoSQL with PySpark, Applied Sciences 2026), X-SLR (Information 2026), OLAP + NoSQL systematic mapping (BDCC 2024), polyglot persistence with Python (Springer 2025), AI-assisted literature reviews with BERT topic clustering (Springer 2025), IEEE ICEDEG 2025. So research-engineer, data-infrastructure, data-pipeline and forward-deployed/solutions roles are realistic, not only SWE. Native Spanish, professional English. Authorized to work in the US. Lives near Oklahoma City; wants remote-US roles or OKC-area on-site/hybrid. Mid-level, not senior/staff. Known gaps: Kubernetes, ML training-data pipelines at very large scale.",
